From 448f3c5d54be6f495b464ec2e600b234b5098715 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: i9 subagent <i9@local>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:31:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(link): route binary scan chunks past the JSON parser
 + scan-payload codec
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The telemetry drain called json.loads() guarded only by
except json.JSONDecodeError; a binary scan datagram containing any byte
>= 0x80 raised UnicodeDecodeError, which escaped telemetry() into the
run.py control loop (v6 §2.5, verified repro). Sniff the spec-v1 magic
byte 0x53 before json.loads and route to the new scan decoder; JSON
datagrams always start with '{' (0x7B), so the sniff is unambiguous.

New scan_payload.py implements wire spec v1 (v6 §2):
- 16 B chunk header (msg/ver_flags/scan_id/chunk_idx/chunk_count/
  first_idx/n_samples/t0_ms/period_us), all multi-byte fields LE
- per-sample angle i8 (-128 = no sample), range_mm u16 (millimetres),
  status u8, optional signal/ambient/t_us u16 gated by header flag bits
- strict decode: version, reserved bit, idx/count, n_samples<=64,
  exact length-vs-header, angle and range bounds raise ScanPayloadError
- chunk_plan() tiles N samples into ceil(N/64) chunks; ScanAssembler
  reports scans with missing chunks as incomplete/partial, never
  silently complete

UDPLink: last_scan / scan_rx / scan_rx_errors attrs, scan_results queue
drained by take_scans(); the JSON telemetry path is otherwise unchanged.
